 ```sh
 DATA_FILE=/srv/tickets/data/tickets.json node /srv/tickets/scripts/weekly-report.js --json > /srv/dashboard/weekly.json
 ```
+
+## Rolling out due times
+
+Back up the production data file, then deploy 1.5.0 with `DUE_TIMES` unset. Startup fills missing
+`due` fields using each ticket's creation time and priority and saves the file before listening.
+A failed save prevents startup. New tickets also get persisted due times while the flag is off.
+Check the file has a `due` timestamp on every ticket, then restart with `DUE_TIMES=on` to expose
+them in API ticket responses and enable the overdue filter.
+
+Response hour settings apply when a due time is first assigned. Priority changes, settings changes
+and restarts preserve that timestamp. Backfilling does not alter ticket history or notifications.
+
+To disable the API feature, unset `DUE_TIMES` and restart. To roll back, stop the service and run
+1.4.0 against the same version 1 data file: it ignores the extra ticket field and reads all tickets.
+Its next save drops due fields; redeploying 1.5.0 after that backfills them again using the response
+hour settings at that time. Keep the backup if the original deadlines must be restored.
